B.bpu=new A.ql(B.ad3,"Flexbox, Grid and tables that behave","Content from a CMS or an email template uses whatever layout the author reached for. Flex and grid containers lay out as containers, and tables get a W3C-style two-pass column algorithm with colspan and rowspan \u2014 not a best-effort approximation.","Same markup a browser would take.",'<div style="display:flex; gap:8px; margin-bottom:12px;">\n  <div style="flex:2; background:#dbeafe; padding:10px; border-radius:6px;">flex: 2</div>\n  <div style="flex:1; background:#bfdbfe; padding:10px; border-radius:6px;">flex: 1</div>\n</div>\n<div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr; gap:8px;\n            margin-bottom:12px;">\n  <div style="background:#e0e7ff; padding:10px; border-radius:6px;">grid</div>\n  <div style="background:#e0e7ff; padding:10px; border-radius:6px;">3 \xd7 1fr</div>\n  <div style="background:#e0e7ff; padding:10px; border-radius:6px;">columns</div>\n</div>\n<table style="border-collapse:collapse; width:100%;">\n  <tr><th colspan="2" style="border:1px solid #94a3b8; padding:6px;\n      background:#f1f5f9;">colspan = 2</th></tr>\n  <tr><td rowspan="2" style="border:1px solid #94a3b8; padding:6px;">rowspan<br/>= 2</td>\n      <td style="border:1px solid #94a3b8; padding:6px;">cell</td></tr>\n  <tr><td style="border:1px solid #94a3b8; padding:6px;">cell</td></tr>\n</table>\n')
B.bpv=new A.ql(B.uP,"A real CSS engine, not a style mapper","The cascade, specificity, inheritance and shorthands are implemented \u2014 so a <style> block behaves the way the author expected, instead of only inline attributes being honoured.","189 CSS declarations handled, counted from the parser source (flutter_html: 51).",'<style>\n  .card { background:#eef2ff; border-left:4px solid #1a56db; padding:12px;\n          border-radius:8px; }\n  .card h4 { color:#1a56db; margin:0 0 6px 0; }\n  .card p  { margin:0; color:#334155; }\n  #special { background:#fef9c3; border-left-color:#ca8a04; }\n  #special h4 { color:#a16207; }\n</style>\n<div class="card"><h4>Class selector</h4><p>Styled from a &lt;style&gt; block.</p></div>\n<div class="card" id="special"><h4>ID beats class</h4>\n  <p>Specificity resolved the way CSS specifies.</p></div>\n')
B.bpw=new A.ql(B.uO,"One document, one selection","Drag across headings, paragraphs, a list and a table below. The selection is continuous because the document is a single RenderObject with one hit-test tree. Renderers built from one widget per tag select per widget, so the same drag fragments at every boundary.","Try it: long-press and drag through the different block types.",'<h3>Select from this heading\u2026</h3>\n<p>\u2026through this paragraph, <strong>past the bold run</strong> and the\n<span style="background:#fff3a3;">highlighted span</span>, without the\nselection breaking apart.</p>\n<ul><li>Into a list item</li><li>And the next one</li></ul>\n<table style="border-collapse:collapse; width:100%;">\n  <tr><td style="border:1px solid #ccc; padding:6px;">\u2026and into</td>\n      <td style="border:1px solid #ccc; padding:6px;">a table cell.</td></tr>\n</table>\n')
B.bpx=new A.ql(B.oz,"Accessible by default",'Headings, links, images and lists are exposed to screen readers with the right roles, and text honours the system "large text" setting the same way a Flutter Text does \u2014 WCAG 2.1 AA \xa71.4.4. Content that refuses to scale is content some users cannot read.',"Semantics tree + text scaling, not an afterthought.",'<h3>A real heading (announced as one)</h3>\n<p>A <a href="https://example.com">link with an accessible name</a>, an image\nwith alt text, and a list \u2014 all exposed with the correct roles.</p>\n<img src="https://picsum.photos/seed/tour_a11y/80/80"\n     alt="Descriptive alt text" style="width:80px; border-radius:6px;" />\n<ol><li>Ordered item one</li><li>Ordered item two</li></ol>\n')
B.bpy=new A.ql(B.oF,"Safe with untrusted HTML","Rendering user-generated or emailed HTML means rendering whatever someone else wrote. Sanitisation is ON by default: scripts never run (there is no JS engine at all), and dangerous URL schemes are blocked before they reach a tap handler or an image loader.","The markup below contains a script tag and a javascript: link \u2014 neither does anything.",'<p>Trusted content renders normally.</p>\n<script>alert(\'this never runs\');</script>\n<p><a href="javascript:alert(\'blocked\')">This link is neutralised</a> \u2014\ntapping it does nothing.</p>\n<img src="javascript:alert(\'blocked\')" alt="blocked image source" />\n<p style="color:#15803d;">Everything above rendered safely.</p>\n')
B.bpz=new A.ql(B.DH,"Ruby annotations & CJK line breaking","Japanese, Chinese and Korean text needs furigana sitting ABOVE the base characters, and line breaks that never strand punctuation at the start of a line (kinsoku shori). Without native ruby, <rt> falls inline beside the base and the reading becomes noise.","Rendered natively \u2014 no WebView, no per-character widget tree.",'<p style="font-size:19px; line-height:2.2;">\n  <ruby>\u6f22\u5b57<rt>\u304b\u3093\u3058</rt></ruby>\u306b<ruby>\u632f<rt>\u3075</rt></ruby>\u308a<ruby>\u4eee\u540d<rt>\u304c\u306a</rt></ruby>\u3092\n  <ruby>\u4ed8<rt>\u3064</rt></ruby>\u3051\u3066<ruby>\u8aad<rt>\u3088</rt></ruby>\u307f\u3084\u3059\u304f\u3057\u307e\u3059\u3002\n</p>\n<p style="font-size:15px; line-height:2;">\n  \u7d04\u7269\uff08\u3001\u3002\u300c\u300d\uff09\u304c\u884c\u982d\u306b\u6765\u306a\u3044\u3088\u3046\u3001\u7981\u5247\u51e6\u7406\u3092\u884c\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002\u65e5\u672c\u8a9e\u306e\u6587\u7ae0\u3067\u3082\n  \u81ea\u7136\u306a\u6539\u884c\u306b\u306a\u308a\u307e\u3059\u3002\n</p>\n')
B.bpA=new A.ql(B.DI,"CSS float \u2014 the one nobody else has","Magazine layouts, blogs and HTML email all wrap text around images. A widget-tree renderer maps each tag to a widget, and a widget cannot know where the previous widget's last line ended \u2014 so the image gets its own row and the text starts below it. HyperRender lays the whole document out on one canvas, so the line breaker knows exactly which space the float occupies.","Verified against flutter_html and FWFH source: neither implements float.",'<img src="https://picsum.photos/seed/tour_float/120/120"\n     style="float:left; width:120px; height:120px; border-radius:10px;\n            margin:0 14px 8px 0;" />\n<p>Text flows around the floated image, line by line, and continues underneath\nonce it runs past the bottom edge \u2014 the same way a browser does it. Resize the\nwindow and the wrap recomputes; the image never sits on a line of its own.</p>\n<p>A second paragraph keeps respecting the same float.</p>\n<div style="clear:both;"></div>\n')
